module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.fci1_control_output_captured_to_journal

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BlockerClassUnstated, RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread }

data fci1_control_output_captured_to_journal: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "fci1_control_output_captured_to_journal" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungUnread { cause: BlockerClassUnstated },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a control that redirects a transient unit's output to a file and then greps that file, where the unit was launched `systemd-run --wait` without `--pipe`. systemd then connects the unit's stdout and stderr to the journal, so the redirect captures nothing and the grep over an empty file fails regardless of what the unit said.",

    "HARM: a RED row (the wrong-WorkingDirectory rows of tools/fabric_ci_fci1_bounded_execution_controls.sh, fci1_run_bounded_driver and fci1_run_bounded_submitter) refused with `ControlRefused: parent wrong-cwd row did not name the workspace-root refusal` although the unit emitted exactly that refusal; the refusal text was in the journal. The rows were byte-identical before gunbc#14142 and had never run green on srv3 (see fci1_controls_unrunnable_under_wrap_policy), so the defect was latent and surfaced the first time the controls ran.",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACT: the evaluator was cleared first (BuildBuddy, cwd /tmp in a capped cgroup: gunbc run exits 2 and prints `error: no workspace root`, which the grep matches), which located the fault at the capture, not the refusal. Receipt: the srv3 diagnostic run posted on gunbc#14130 by the lane owner (stern-bat-401): without --pipe the captured file is 0 bytes and the refusal is in the journal; with --pipe it is delivered; the positive control exits 0.",

    "RECOGNITION RULE: a systemd-run --wait (or --collect) launcher whose caller redirects or captures the unit's stdout/stderr; the launcher must carry --pipe. The emitted runners are the one producer (gunbc.fabric.fci1_bounded_execution_context_emit expected_fci1_bounded_execution_context_env), and the witness every_emitted_fci1_runner_pipes_the_unit_output_to_the_caller discriminates it.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: silent-to-the-control, loud-at-the-gate (the row refused, with a misleading cause). CEILING: mechanically preventable (a generated witness over the one emitter); structurally guaranteed once the controls run as the typed actuator, whose launcher option list carries Pipe in one place (gunbc.instruments.fabric_ci_fci1_bounded_controls_actuator fci1_unit_command). NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: the actuator landing and replacing the shell controls.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
